WEBVTT

00:02.700 --> 00:05.925
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:06.171 --> 00:09.456
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:09.491 --> 00:13.010
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:13.061 --> 00:16.014
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:16.048 --> 00:19.518
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:19.569 --> 00:22.821
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:22.855 --> 00:24.406
♪ All the things that make us

00:24.440 --> 00:25.774
♪ Laugh and cry

00:25.808 --> 00:29.230
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.236 --> 00:38.788
<i>ANNOUNCER:
We now return to Bottom Chef.</i>

00:38.822 --> 00:41.357
Daniel L.,
please pack your fudge and go.

00:41.391 --> 00:42.942
Fine!

00:42.976 --> 00:45.261
TOM TUCKER: We interrupt this
broadcast with breaking news.

00:45.295 --> 00:47.563
An aide to Mayor
Adam West has been found

00:47.598 --> 00:49.398
stabbed to death
at the mayor's mansion.

00:49.433 --> 00:50.383
That's right, Tom.

00:50.417 --> 00:51.667
Police say the
victim was killed

00:51.702 --> 00:53.536
by a knife
belonging to the mayor,

00:53.570 --> 00:56.239
who is considered the
prime suspect at this time.

00:56.273 --> 00:57.440
Oh, my God.

00:57.474 --> 00:58.559
Uncle Adam!

00:58.610 --> 00:59.593
Uhp, town emergency.

00:59.627 --> 01:00.877
Don't got to
finish my green beans.

01:00.912 --> 01:03.280
Peter, you stay there and
finish those green beans.

01:03.314 --> 01:06.633
But my stomach's upset
on account of the news.

01:06.668 --> 01:08.368
Also found
in the mayor's residence

01:08.403 --> 01:10.237
was a blackmail note
from the victim

01:10.271 --> 01:11.738
threatening to expose the mayor

01:11.773 --> 01:14.508
in a corruption scandal
unless the victim was paid off.

01:14.542 --> 01:16.143
You can put a picture of a note

01:16.177 --> 01:18.412
above my shoulder any time now,
Tony.

01:18.446 --> 01:20.448
No, that's the Rose Bowl Parade.

01:20.482 --> 01:22.317
That's the Pumpkin Festival.

01:22.351 --> 01:24.619
Okay, okay,
you think that humiliates me?

01:24.653 --> 01:25.687
You-- I-I don't care.

01:25.721 --> 01:26.921
Oscar De La Hoya does it.

01:26.956 --> 01:28.690
We now go live to
Tricia Takanawa,

01:28.724 --> 01:30.758
who is outside
the mayor's mansion.

01:30.793 --> 01:33.728
Tom, I'm standing outside
the mayor's mansion,

01:33.762 --> 01:35.880
where, against the wishes
of his attorneys,

01:35.914 --> 01:39.267
the mayor has agreed to an
impromptu press conference.

01:39.301 --> 01:41.102
(reporters calling out)

01:41.136 --> 01:42.187
What do you
know about the murder?

01:42.221 --> 01:43.622
Did you
kill that man?

01:43.657 --> 01:45.591
Yes, I'll take a question
from the reporter

01:45.625 --> 01:48.477
<i>from the Quahog
Elementary School Gazette.</i>

01:48.511 --> 01:49.478
Timmy?

01:49.512 --> 01:51.213
Are you afraid of the dark?

01:51.247 --> 01:53.015
I thought
we had an understanding

01:53.049 --> 01:54.783
that the dark was off limits.

01:54.818 --> 01:57.169
This press conference is over.

01:57.203 --> 02:00.205
This has been
Tricia Takanawa with the news.

02:00.239 --> 02:02.941
And now I will have
my normal post-news review

02:02.976 --> 02:04.911
from my mom in her car.

02:04.945 --> 02:06.112
You no good!

02:06.147 --> 02:07.447
You no good on news!

02:07.481 --> 02:09.382
You stiff, like
watching board!

02:09.417 --> 02:11.151
Joan London
mother, so happy.

02:11.185 --> 02:14.654
Tricia Takanawa
mother, so sad.

02:14.689 --> 02:16.489
Wow, he really did it.

02:16.524 --> 02:18.391
I always knew Mayor West
was a little crazy,

02:18.426 --> 02:20.994
but I never thought he was
capable of something like this.

02:21.028 --> 02:22.629
The mayor's going to jail.

02:22.663 --> 02:24.547
That means anything goes.

02:25.634 --> 02:28.719
(knocking on door)

02:28.754 --> 02:30.438
I pushed a lady.

02:30.472 --> 02:32.390
God, I can already
hear the jokes

02:32.424 --> 02:34.508
Jay Leno's gonna be
telling about our mayor.

02:34.543 --> 02:35.543
Oh, yeah,
like what?

02:35.577 --> 02:36.661
Oh, you know,

02:36.712 --> 02:37.878
it's like you can
already hear them.

02:37.913 --> 02:38.996
You know?
Like what?

02:39.047 --> 02:40.447
Like exactly
what jokes do you hear?

02:40.465 --> 02:41.832
Tell me one of the jokes.

02:41.883 --> 02:44.001
Brian, all I have to do is
start fake sneezing around you

02:44.036 --> 02:46.520
and you'll spend the rest
of your life outside.

02:46.555 --> 02:48.690
Oh, yeah, yeah, I can
hear some of the jokes.

02:48.725 --> 02:50.175
Well, I guess
you just never know

02:50.209 --> 02:52.594
what kind of rage
some people have bottled up.

02:52.628 --> 02:54.012
Well, we all
got anger, Chris.

02:54.047 --> 02:55.047
The important thing

02:55.081 --> 02:56.848
is finding a healthy way
to channel it.

02:56.899 --> 02:59.568
For me, as you know,
it's the family bath.

02:59.602 --> 03:01.803
Peter, how long
do we have to sit here?

03:01.838 --> 03:03.205
Until I'm
not angry anymore,

03:03.239 --> 03:05.273
you naked
bunch of bitches!

03:05.308 --> 03:06.658
(seagulls squawking)

03:09.028 --> 03:11.097
(indistinct chatter)

03:17.271 --> 03:19.188
JUDGE: Everyone,
please be seated.

03:19.223 --> 03:20.623
We will now hear

03:20.657 --> 03:22.759
the defense attorney's
closing statement.

03:22.793 --> 03:24.160
I switched seats.

03:24.194 --> 03:26.529
In closing, although
it seems pretty clear

03:26.563 --> 03:28.164
that my client
committed this murder,

03:28.198 --> 03:29.932
I would consider it
a personal favor to me

03:29.967 --> 03:31.552
if you found
him not guilty.

03:31.603 --> 03:34.855
That's your
closing argument?

03:34.889 --> 03:38.709
Whoa, those karate
lessons are really paying off.

03:38.743 --> 03:40.744
Thank you, Sensei.

03:40.779 --> 03:41.879
Welcome.

03:41.913 --> 03:43.013
He came.

03:43.047 --> 03:44.598
Jurors, you
have now heard

03:44.632 --> 03:46.066
all the facts
of this case.

03:46.101 --> 03:48.602
I remind you that because
we are a small town,

03:48.636 --> 03:49.937
many of you may have ties

03:49.971 --> 03:51.672
with the defendant
or the victim.

03:51.706 --> 03:53.925
You must set aside
these personal connections

03:53.959 --> 03:56.461
and render an impartial
and unanimous verdict.

03:56.495 --> 03:58.096
Does anyone have any questions?

03:58.130 --> 04:01.266
Yeah, is Toblerone
the fanciest thing in the world?

04:01.300 --> 04:02.534
I-I just don't understand.

04:02.568 --> 04:04.152
How could
Uncle Adam do this?

04:04.186 --> 04:05.787
He's the mayor
of our town.

04:05.821 --> 04:08.022
Well, Meg, life
isn't always as simple

04:08.057 --> 04:09.691
as what they
teach you at school.

04:09.725 --> 04:10.759
I don't know, Mom.

04:10.793 --> 04:12.927
I have a pretty realistic
home ec class.

04:12.962 --> 04:14.362
Okay, kids.

04:14.396 --> 04:17.500
Now I'm gonna take
the casserole out of the oven.

04:17.534 --> 04:19.218
Okay, it's a little burned.

04:19.252 --> 04:20.669
No reason to panic.

04:20.704 --> 04:22.171
(tires screech, car
door opens and closes)

04:22.205 --> 04:23.172
Oh, God, that's Daddy.

04:23.206 --> 04:24.523
He's home early.

04:24.557 --> 04:26.325
Let-Let's get some spices
in here and fix this.

04:26.359 --> 04:27.326
(door opens
and closes)

04:27.360 --> 04:28.560
Okay, he's inside the house.

04:28.578 --> 04:29.912
Let's-let's hope his meeting
went well.

04:29.946 --> 04:31.747
MAN: God, that meeting
went awful!

04:31.782 --> 04:32.782
Oh, boy.

04:32.816 --> 04:33.849
What's that smell?

04:33.884 --> 04:35.284
Did you burn dinner,
you stupid pig?

04:35.318 --> 04:36.568
Okay, kids, put your heads down.

04:36.586 --> 04:37.587
Put your heads down.

04:37.622 --> 04:38.889
And don't try to stand between

04:38.923 --> 04:40.690
me and your father;
it'll just make it worse.

04:46.747 --> 04:49.583
So I's been asked by the judge
to be the foreman,

04:49.617 --> 04:51.651
and I want y'all to know
that we's gonna run

04:51.686 --> 04:55.589
a fair jury and a clean jury,
so I brought some wet naps

04:55.623 --> 04:57.824
for everyone to wipe off
their areas.

04:57.859 --> 05:00.995
'Cause one of us gets sick,
we's all gonna get sick.

05:01.029 --> 05:02.430
And that may lead to some of us

05:02.464 --> 05:03.998
getting sicker than others.

05:04.032 --> 05:05.433
Look, can we
get this underway?

05:05.467 --> 05:06.901
I mean, we were
all in that courtroom.

05:06.935 --> 05:08.135
What-what is
there to discuss?

05:08.170 --> 05:09.170
It's obvious
he did it.

05:09.238 --> 05:11.756
(overlapping chatter)

05:11.807 --> 05:13.327
Plus, I got to get
back to the station.

05:13.342 --> 05:14.609
If I'm not there by 5:00,

05:14.643 --> 05:15.977
Joyce will anchor the news,
and I don't think

05:16.011 --> 05:17.879
anyone wants
that to happen again.

05:17.913 --> 05:20.548
Our top story:
Guys, right?

05:20.582 --> 05:21.917
Yes, it's open and shut.

05:21.951 --> 05:23.986
Now let's just vote him guilty
and get out of here.

05:24.020 --> 05:25.381
Look, I know
everyone's in a hurry,

05:25.388 --> 05:27.256
but shouldn't we at least
go over the evidence

05:27.290 --> 05:29.291
once before we vote,
just to be fair?

05:29.325 --> 05:31.460
You know what would shed
some light on th case?

05:31.494 --> 05:33.612
If we huck water balloons
at people in the street.

05:36.282 --> 05:38.016
They were carrying a trampoline.

05:38.051 --> 05:39.084
Here's the facts:

05:39.118 --> 05:40.686
there was a note
from the victim,

05:40.720 --> 05:43.690
threatening to expose the mayor
in a corruption scandal.

05:43.724 --> 05:46.342
The murder weapon
was the mayor's own knife.

05:46.377 --> 05:49.812
And finally, that lady with
the Peter Gallagher eyebrows

05:49.847 --> 05:52.582
on the witness stand
saw the whole thing.

05:52.616 --> 05:53.896
Okay, let's get
down to business.

05:53.918 --> 05:56.152
All in favor of "guilty,"
raise your hands.

05:56.186 --> 05:57.420
(together):
Guilty.

05:57.454 --> 05:58.788
All "guilty."

05:58.822 --> 05:59.989
Good, well, that's it,
let's get out of here.

06:00.024 --> 06:01.624
Anyone for "not guilty"?

06:06.464 --> 06:09.016
(angry, incredulous remarks)

06:09.050 --> 06:10.434
What the hell?

06:10.468 --> 06:13.003
All right, looks like
we's gonna be here a while.

06:13.038 --> 06:14.505
Who wants pizza for dinner?

06:15.824 --> 06:18.959
And who wants
Purina Moist and Meaty Dog Chow?

06:20.495 --> 06:23.364
(angry, incredulous remarks)

06:23.398 --> 06:24.732
I had that
for breakfast!

06:31.461 --> 06:32.701
What do you mean "not guilty"?!

06:32.712 --> 06:33.679
What's wrong with you?

06:33.713 --> 06:35.781
Oh, shoot,
that was a stomachache.

06:35.815 --> 06:37.249
I told that guy he had polio.

06:37.283 --> 06:39.484
Look, the system specifies
the defendant

06:39.519 --> 06:42.187
must be proven guilty
beyond a reasonable doubt.

06:42.221 --> 06:44.256
Mayor West's life
is on the line here.

06:44.290 --> 06:46.425
I'm just saying,
it's possible he didn't do it.

06:46.459 --> 06:48.042
(angry, incredulous remarks)

06:48.061 --> 06:49.679
That's for the jury
to decide.

06:49.713 --> 06:51.264
Mayor West is crazy.

06:51.298 --> 06:53.516
He should've been locked up
a long time ago.

06:53.550 --> 06:55.351
Yeah, there's definitely
something off about him.

06:55.386 --> 06:56.452
I'm his physician.

06:56.487 --> 06:59.255
Okay, now we'll just
test those reflexes.

06:59.289 --> 07:00.623
MAN (muffled):
Hey, did you hear that?

07:00.657 --> 07:01.657
MAN 2:
There's someone out there.

07:01.692 --> 07:02.759
Hello?

07:02.793 --> 07:04.093
WOMAN (muffled):
We're in here!

07:04.128 --> 07:05.528
MAN 3:
There are six of us!

07:05.596 --> 07:07.580
Look, we all saw
that blackmail note.

07:07.614 --> 07:09.382
Mayor West is
the only one with a motive.

07:09.416 --> 07:10.818
I don't even know
why we're discussing it.

07:10.852 --> 07:13.437
Well, was Mayor West
the only one with a motive?

07:13.471 --> 07:15.205
I mean, there are
people who would benefit

07:15.240 --> 07:16.640
if he were
put away for murder.

07:16.674 --> 07:18.525
Political rivals,
special interests.

07:18.560 --> 07:20.511
I mean, it's possible
he could have been framed.

07:20.545 --> 07:23.514
(angry, incredulous remarks)

07:23.548 --> 07:25.165
Enough!

07:25.200 --> 07:27.267
Was a movie with Jennifer Lopez

07:27.302 --> 07:29.336
that did not
live up to expectations.

07:29.338 --> 07:32.339
Well, Mayor West did say
he never saw the letter.

07:32.373 --> 07:33.641
And he was under oath.

07:33.676 --> 07:34.676
Yeah, he lied.

07:34.710 --> 07:36.327
Of course he lied;
he's a politician.

07:36.362 --> 07:37.729
They're all liars.
Yeah!

07:37.763 --> 07:40.215
John F. Kennedy swore he'd serve
a full four-year term.

07:40.249 --> 07:41.649
Liar.

07:41.684 --> 07:44.452
Look, we should be sticking
to the facts, not stereotypes.

07:44.487 --> 07:47.405
It's unfair to say
that all politicians are liars,

07:47.439 --> 07:49.073
therefore Mayor West is guilty.

07:49.107 --> 07:50.425
Brian's right.

07:50.459 --> 07:53.561
I was a county alderman once
and I never told no fibs.

07:53.596 --> 07:55.464
I bent over
backwards and forwards

07:55.499 --> 07:56.766
for them constituents.

07:56.800 --> 07:59.001
It's important
to make sure everyone is happy,

07:59.035 --> 08:00.770
so I took a lot of polls.

08:00.804 --> 08:02.104
(muttering):
Gay stuff.

08:02.139 --> 08:04.940
Yeah, and I served honorably
as a U.N. interpreter.

08:04.975 --> 08:07.376
(speaking foreign language)

08:07.410 --> 08:09.245
Okay, he's mad about something.

08:09.279 --> 08:11.413
He appears to be
talking really fast.

08:11.448 --> 08:14.183
He spits whenever
he makes the "ch" noise,

08:14.217 --> 08:16.753
which, in this language,
happens a lot.

08:16.788 --> 08:18.889
I'm expected to entertain him
and his wife tonight,

08:18.923 --> 08:21.258
so if anyone knows a good
restaurant in the area...

08:21.292 --> 08:23.426
Sushi or tapas,
something where they're always

08:23.461 --> 08:24.578
bringing stuff to the table

08:24.612 --> 08:25.879
so you have something
to talk about.

08:25.913 --> 08:27.080
You know?

08:27.114 --> 08:28.682
"Hey, what's this?
This looks good..."

08:28.716 --> 08:29.950
War, oh, war, war!

08:29.984 --> 08:31.902
That last sentence
was about war!

08:31.936 --> 08:33.653
Look, an expert
confirmed

08:33.688 --> 08:35.655
that the blackmail note
was signed by the victim.

08:35.690 --> 08:37.757
That points
irrefutably to West.

08:37.792 --> 08:39.927
Well, maybe we should
take a look at that letter.

08:39.962 --> 08:41.262
Yeah, I'd like to see that.

08:41.296 --> 08:43.731
'Cause I can read it
just like everybody else.

08:43.765 --> 08:46.000
<i>And the charade continues.</i>

08:46.034 --> 08:48.386
Bailiff, please.

08:48.437 --> 08:49.503
Yeah?

08:49.521 --> 08:51.439
Mr. Bailiff, we
request that you

08:51.473 --> 08:53.074
bring us the note
from the victim.

08:53.108 --> 08:55.126
Joe, what the hell
are you doing out there?

08:55.160 --> 08:56.727
You're a cop, not a bailiff.

08:56.762 --> 08:57.962
Eh, I'm undercover.

08:57.996 --> 08:59.797
Someone's been raping
all the bailiffs.

08:59.832 --> 09:02.134
So you're just sitting around
waiting to be raped?

09:02.168 --> 09:03.836
MAN (gruffly): Hey, Bailiff,
can I talk to you

09:03.870 --> 09:05.671
for a second in
this broom closet?

09:05.705 --> 09:06.939
Sure, strange man.

09:06.973 --> 09:10.676
I can't wait to hear
what this is all about.

09:16.032 --> 09:17.416
Well, there's your motive.

09:17.467 --> 09:19.484
A note from the victim
threatening Mayor West.

09:19.519 --> 09:20.853
What more proof
do you want?

09:20.887 --> 09:22.822
Yeah, are you trying to
suggest that Mayor West's

09:22.857 --> 09:24.324
enemy faked
a corruption letter

09:24.358 --> 09:25.425
and then
killed himself?

09:25.459 --> 09:26.459
That's idiotic!

09:29.380 --> 09:32.282
But it just might work.

09:32.316 --> 09:33.383
What?

09:39.924 --> 09:41.291
You know, something bothered me

09:41.325 --> 09:42.959
about the stationery
that note was on,

09:42.993 --> 09:44.595
with the-the decorative
"M" border.

09:44.629 --> 09:45.629
It's from the
office of the mayor.

09:45.664 --> 09:46.664
The "M" is for "mayor."

09:46.698 --> 09:48.232
What are you
getting at?

09:48.266 --> 09:50.067
No, no, I'm pretty sure
the "M" is for "Marriott."

09:50.101 --> 09:52.036
How do you know?
Because I once got a note

09:52.070 --> 09:56.173
from the Marriott
written on the same paper.

09:56.207 --> 09:57.541
(gasping)

09:57.576 --> 09:58.909
"Dear Brian.

09:58.944 --> 10:00.394
"You were amazing last night.

10:00.428 --> 10:01.562
Love, Ida."

10:01.596 --> 10:02.796
(laughing):
This is from the night

10:02.847 --> 10:04.815
you had sex with Quagmire's dad.

10:04.849 --> 10:06.066
Ah, come on!

10:06.101 --> 10:08.503
I did a dog once,
but I was in the Philippines,

10:08.537 --> 10:10.038
and I sure as hell
didn't write him a letter.

10:10.072 --> 10:11.907
What's-- w-w-what, so
what does that prove?

10:11.974 --> 10:13.041
The victim had access

10:13.075 --> 10:14.376
to all the "Office of the Mayor"

10:14.410 --> 10:15.677
stationery he could ever want,

10:15.711 --> 10:17.612
yet he hand-made a letterhead

10:17.647 --> 10:19.614
on stationery from a Marriott?

10:19.649 --> 10:21.449
As far as I'm concerned,
that casts doubt.

10:21.484 --> 10:24.102
(angry, incredulous remarks)

10:24.136 --> 10:25.520
Look, you guys
just say the word

10:25.554 --> 10:27.539
and I'll put this ball with
cheese in it on the floor.

10:27.573 --> 10:29.558
We won't hear from him
for an hour and a half.

10:32.613 --> 10:35.164
Look, if I'm still the only
one who says "not guilty,"

10:35.198 --> 10:37.099
I won't hold
things up any longer.

10:37.134 --> 10:38.918
Let's vote again,
and I'll abstain.

10:38.952 --> 10:40.152
If it's unanimous,

10:40.187 --> 10:42.104
I'll change my vote
and we can all go home.

10:42.139 --> 10:45.274
Okay, everyone take one of these
here and write their vote.

10:47.661 --> 10:50.998
Hey, Quagmire, y-you gonna
write something funny?

10:51.032 --> 10:52.366
No, Peter, I'm not.

10:52.400 --> 10:54.601
I'm starting to think
all you do is dick around.

10:54.635 --> 10:56.536
Sorry.

10:57.722 --> 10:59.473
Everyone vote?

10:59.507 --> 11:01.274
Okay, now let's count.

11:01.309 --> 11:04.161
"Guilty," "guilty."

11:04.195 --> 11:07.030
Some hurtful slurs followed
by the word "guilty."

11:07.065 --> 11:08.031
(laughs)

11:08.066 --> 11:10.434
"Guilty," "guilty."

11:10.468 --> 11:12.069
"El guilto."

11:12.103 --> 11:14.272
"Guilty," "guilty."

11:14.306 --> 11:16.557
This one's just a squiggly line.

11:16.592 --> 11:19.794
That's, uh,
that's "guilty" in Latin.

11:19.828 --> 11:22.397
<i>You're playing
a dangerous game, Carl.</i>

11:22.431 --> 11:23.731
"Guilty."

11:23.766 --> 11:25.633
